# Copy to server/.env and fill in as needed. Never commit the real server/.env
# file. This example does not attempt to enumerate every backend variable
# (see server/.env for the full set already in use, e.g. MONGO_URI,
# GROQ_API_KEY, COGNITO_*, S3, Ably) - it currently documents only
# the routing and CORS additions below.

# ─── CORS (browser-origin allowlist) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed to call this API (see
# server/server.js). Defaults to http://localhost:3000 (this project's CRA
# dev origin) if unset, so local development works with no configuration.
# Requests with no Origin header (curl, server-to-server calls, health
# checks) are always allowed - only browser-sent Origins are checked.
#
# Set this in production to your real deployed frontend origin(s). This repo
# does not hardcode a production URL because it isn't confirmed which host
# (Netlify/Vercel/a custom domain) actually serves the frontend - see
# server/server.js's CORS comment. Example:
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-production-frontend.example.com
# Multiple origins (e.g. a staging site too) are supported, comma-separated:
#   ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-production-frontend.example.com,https://staging.example.com
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000

# ─── ROUTING (Valhalla, self-hosted) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# URL of a self-hosted Valhalla instance - see
# server/tools/README-routing-setup.md for how to build and run one locally
# (Docker). No API key: this is never a public/paid service. Env controls
# deployment - there is no hardcoded fallback in application code, so
# /api/routing/* requests fail cleanly (503) if this isn't set.
VALHALLA_URL=http://localhost:8002

# ─── S3 PROVIDER (server/services/s3Provider.js) ─────────────────────────────
# Which S3 backend to use. Real AWS still needs its usual variables
# (APP_AWS_REGION, APP_AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID/SECRET, PROPERTY_IMAGES_ACCESS_KEY/
# SECRET, S3_BUCKET_NAME, APP_S3_BUCKET_PROPERTY_IMAGES) already documented
# in server/.env - S3_MODE only chooses which backend those requests go to.
#
#   aws   - always AWS, never checks/uses Floci.
#   floci - always Floci (local S3-compatible emulator), never checks/uses AWS.
#   auto  - (default if unset) AWS preferred: checks AWS config + does a
#           live availability check once at startup; falls back to Floci
#           only if AWS is unconfigured or that check fails. Whichever
#           provider is picked is locked for the life of the server process
#           - a later AWS operation failure never causes a runtime switch.
S3_MODE=auto

# Local Floci endpoint (only used when S3_MODE=floci, or when S3_MODE=auto
# falls back to Floci). Floci never receives real AWS credentials - dummy
# values are used automatically.
FLOCI_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4566
